---
import Basic from "../../components/BasicPage.astro";
import PlaceholderImage from "../../components/PlaceholderImage.astro";
import Judgment from "../../media/bunger/FTRookie_judge.png";

//todo: write something about my ai usage policy
// summary: i'm an ideas guy, ai is the pattern and syntax recognizer
// it's a good research tool, but to trust it to design things entirely will lead to nonsense
// ai is still not good at logic, but it's faster than humans for simple things like syntax
---

<Basic title="Coding" favicon={Judgment} backHref="/likes">
    <div id="content">
        <h2>Coding isn't my favorite thing in the world, but I tolerate it</h2>
        <p>
            I like to be able to create things, and for that reason, coding is a
            great way to put ideas into practice with very little investment
            involved.
        </p>
        <p>
            I've experimented in a lot of ways, usually via Roblox Studio just
            trying to make the framework for a game, but can never find myself
            committing to it for very long.
        </p>
        <PlaceholderImage />
    </div>
    <div id="info">
        <h2>Some languages I have used <br />Most to Least used</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Luau (Roblox)</li>
            <li>Python</li>
            <li>Javascript</li>
            <li>Typescript</li>
            <li>Java</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</Basic>
